  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 116 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nH-O-T. A strong, zonally oriented upper-level ridge along the US \nSouth features 500mb heights to near 600 dam, especially \npronounced from the Desert Southwest and east along the Gulf \nCoast. Heights over our region are near seasonal maximum values, \nwhich supports the continued surface temps in the mid 90s. A \nfrontal boundary retreats northward today as low-level flow has \nturned out of the southwest. With dew points in the low to mid 70s\nstill, western 2/3rds of our forecast area will see heat index \nvalues top out around 105 degrees again.\n\nAs the ridge comes to amplify over western/central CONUS this\nweekend, troughing will deepen along the East Coast, and flow\naloft will turn more sharply out of the northwest. Rain chances\nthrough the next few days, will be primarily confined to northeast\nor eastern most portions of our area. Rain chances next week are\nlimited by the ridge aloft, but a wave may pass through the area\nmid week and trigger some shower and thunderstorm activity.\n\nThe main threat will be heat amplifying beneath the ridge. Today\nand tomorrow's \"Limited\" heat stress with 105 heat index values\nwill yield to \"Significant\" heat stress with actual air \ntemperatures in the upper 90s to near 100 degrees Monday through \nThursday with peak heat index values across the board in the 110 \nto 115 range. As always, at this time of year, please make sure \nloved ones, neighbors, and pets have a cool place to spend the hot\nafternoons and warm nights. /NF/",
